      "sourceTextSha256": "1a5511afc3126795e25d154867e4cbe438df127aa90c06142d55942b0320c99d",
      "text": "We will leave early in the morning to visit Atlixco, known as \"the city of flowers\" for its production of flowers and ornamental plants. Its historic center is charming, full of colorful colonial houses, churches and picturesque squares \n\nIn the afternoon we return to Mexico City to visit Mixquic, its streets are filled with altars adorned with flowers, candles and personal items in honor of the deceased, one of the most emblematic traditions is the visit to the local cemetery, where families decorate the graves and spend the night there, accompanied by food and music. \n\nRoyal Reforma www.hotelroyalreforma.com 3 Night / Std-Room ",
