    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4b90b47ca61bef81dacd1a4e1a4ebd0fdab9066f4f541648422e47a932080b94",
      "text": "Today we head to the south of the city, where we will visit the Barrio de San Angel, a neighborhood that is known for its cobblestone streets, colonial architecture and bohemian atmosphere. Here we will visit the Diego Rivera House Studio, where the famous muralist lived and worked. \n\nWe'll continue our tour to the Ciudad Universitaria (CU), renowned for its modernist architecture and murals by artists such as Rivera and Siqueiros. \n\nBoat ride through the canals of Xochimilco, famous for its canals and floating gardens. \n\nIn the afternoon, we return to the hotel. ",
